# Line-ending policy, pinned so behavior does not depend on each clone's
# core.autocrlf setting (which otherwise produces phantom "modified" files with
# empty diffs). LF is canonical in the repository AND in the working tree on
# every platform, including Windows.
#
# Why LF in the working tree: the generators, test harnesses, and editors that
# write into this repo all emit LF. A CRLF working tree turns every such write
# into an LF island inside a CRLF file, and because the index normalizes to LF
# the resulting mixed-ending file is invisible to `git diff` while breaking
# mid-line in Windows editors. Pinning eol=lf keeps the two in agreement.
# `.githooks/pre-commit` rejects staged files with mixed endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets, never apply EOL conversion.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
